 structure. Opening a different document or editing the result removes the old
 trajectory association. Model hosts control whether snapshots are recorded,
 their retention, and access to the trajectory file.
+
+### Patched document ownership and persistence
+
+`renderFrame` is display-only: picks do not address the editable document until `showDocument` or `openSession` restores it. Use `openSession` to edit a different result; there is no assumed frame index mapping. Mol* overlays remain display-only. Document-local indices are not original-source identities.
+
+Session responses include `persistence.state`: `saved`, `ephemeral`, or `memory_only`. A memory-committed edit whose disk snapshot failed returns its actual structure/revision with `memory_only`, not a false rollback. Export immediately or POST `/api/v1/sessions/{session_id}/persistence/retry`; unsaved and active sessions are not pruned. This is not durable project storage, and restart does not restore Undo/revision.
+
+Activate a sequence segment button to edit its length and explicit before/after anchor. `/segments/edit` takes the segment's current `atom_index`, bounds, optional `anchor_index`, `before`, and `expected_revision`. Moves are one Undo transaction and preserve atom/pair annotations. Structural residue IDs are reordered for parseable export; author identity annotations are retained.
